Workers Rights 

Workers rights are an important part of running a successful buisness. Amazon and Ebay have some rules and policies to protect workers, but there are still areas that need improvment.
According to "Ethcal Consumer", Amazon has faced criticism over its treatment of imployees. In 2024, the GMB trade union took Amazon tocourt claims that workers were pressured leave their union. Amazon explained that its meeting were voluntary, 
and were there to help employees make their own decisions. 
Ebay also has Supplier Code of Conduct, which sets bacis rules for worker treatment. This is a positive step but its not covering everything, such as fair living wages and working hours. The also has faced criticism over trade union issues.
In my opinion, both of companies should protect their employees, they should offer fair pay, safe working conditions and respect workers rights, this would help create a better and fairer workplace. 
